Restrict sine to $-\frac{\pi}{2}\le x\le\frac{\pi}{2}$, where it is one-to-one and has range $[-1,1]$. Reflecting this restricted graph in $y=x$ exchanges its domain and range.

Domain: $-1\le x\le1$.
Range: $-\frac{\pi}{2}\le y\le\frac{\pi}{2}$.

The graph increases from $(-1,-\frac{\pi}{2})$ to $(1,\frac{\pi}{2})$. It is odd because $\arcsin(-x)=-\arcsin x$, and it has no asymptotes.

