Restrict cosine to $0\le x\le\pi$, where it is one-to-one and has range $[-1,1]$. Its inverse exchanges this domain and range.

Domain: $-1\le x\le1$.
Range: $0\le y\le\pi$.

The endpoints are $(-1,\pi)$ and $(1,0)$, and the graph is decreasing. Since $\arccos0=\frac{\pi}{2}\ne0$, it is not odd. Since $\arccos(-1)=\pi\ne\arccos1$, it is not even. It has no asymptotes.

